Credits

  The clock display follows the LEDitron idea by Axiris: seven-segment digits built from LED
  filaments (Elektor Labs, 2015; Elektor magazine, September 2016). Only the idea and the name are
  borrowed; none of Axiris's files are used or included.

  Bluetooth audio uses the ESP32-A2DP library by Phil Schatzmann (Apache License 2.0), fetched at
  build time.

  LLOYDS and TM-838 are the names of the original radio and its maker, used here only to identify
  the set this build is based on.
